# HP LaserJet 1020 (host-based / GDI printer): upload the runtime firmware
# (sihp1020.dl) into the printer's RAM every time it is attached or powered on.
#
# This replaces the RUN+="hplj1020" hook from printer-driver-foo2zjs's
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/85-hplj10xx.rules. That helper uploads in a backgrounded
# subshell and returns immediately, so systemd-udevd (>= 255.4-1ubuntu8.18)
# reaps the worker process group and kills the transfer before it completes.
# Handing the work to a systemd unit decouples it from the udev worker's
# lifetime. scripts/install-firmware-loader.sh disables the stock RUN hook and
# keeps the stock SYMLINK, so this rule only needs to start the service.

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", \
  ATTR{idVendor}=="03f0", ATTR{idProduct}=="2b17", \
  RUN+="/bin/systemctl --no-block --no-ask-password start hplj1020-firmware.service"
